{
  "analysis": "The sed fix for _FILE_minimal worked. The compilation fails because `-msoft-float` makes glibc headers look for `gnu/stubs-o32_soft.h` which doesn't exist (only hard-float glibc is installed). I need to create this missing stubs header. The sysroot is `/`, and the headers are likely at `/usr/mipsel-linux-gnu/include/`.",
  "plan": "Find the gnu/stubs.h file location, create an empty gnu/stubs-o32_soft.h to satisfy the include, then test compilation with -msoft-float again.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "find /usr/mipsel-linux-gnu/include /usr/include -name 'stubs.h' -path '*/gnu/*' 2>/dev/null | head -5\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /usr/mipsel-linux-gnu/include/gnu/stubs.h 2>/dev/null | head -20 || cat /usr/include/gnu/stubs.h 2>/dev/null | head -20\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "touch /usr/mipsel-linux-gnu/include/gnu/stubs-o32_soft.h 2>/dev/null && echo \"created stubs-o32_soft.h\" || echo \"failed to create\"\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '#include <stdio.h>\\nint x;\\n' > /tmp/stest.c && mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -O2 -EL -march=mips32 -msoft-float -mno-abicalls -fno-pic -ffreestanding -nostdlib -fno-builtin -c /tmp/stest.c -o /tmp/stest.o 2>&1 | head -20; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
